From bc69c8663ac9590801a0c870bee36c8a19b4577b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Konrad Dybcio <konrad.dybcio@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 22:45:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 74/85] thunderbolt: tb: Retry USB3 tunnel activation on resume
 completion

Re-activating a USB3 tunnel starts with a bandwidth allocation, which
requires the host controller to acknowledge the Connection Manager
request (ADP_USB3_CS_1.HCA). This happens from the resume_noirq phase.

On platforms where the xHCI is a separate device that is not part of
the host router (e.g. Qualcomm Glymur), it is only resumed later in the
regular resume phase. The HCA wait then times out, the tunnel paths are
never activated and the error goes unnoticed, leaving any tunneled USB3
devices disconnected after resume.

Retry activating any USB3 tunnels that are not active from the
.complete() callback, at which point all devices have been resumed.

Assisted-by: LLM
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/thunderbolt/tb.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/thunderbolt/tb.c b/drivers/thunderbolt/tb.c
index 4da608ccbccb..8e5492e1069f 100644
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/tb.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/tb.c
@@ -3249,6 +3249,26 @@ static int tb_thaw_noirq(struct tb *tb)
 
 static void tb_complete(struct tb *tb)
 {
+	struct tb_cm *tcm = tb_priv(tb);
+	struct tb_tunnel *tunnel, *n;
+
+	/*
+	 * Re-activating a USB3 tunnel needs the host controller to ack the
+	 * bandwidth request (HCA). With the xHCI living outside of the
+	 * router, it may not have resumed yet back in the noirq phase, so
+	 * retry any USB3 tunnels that didn't come up then.
+	 */
+	scoped_guard(mutex, &tb->lock) {
+		list_for_each_entry_safe(tunnel, n, &tcm->tunnel_list, list) {
+			if (!tb_tunnel_is_usb3(tunnel) || tb_tunnel_is_active(tunnel))
+				continue;
+
+			tb_tunnel_dbg(tunnel, "retrying activation after resume\n");
+			if (tb_tunnel_activate(tunnel))
+				tb_tunnel_warn(tunnel, "activation retry failed\n");
+		}
+	}
+
 	/*
 	 * Unregister unplugged XDomains and if there is a case where
 	 * another domain is swapped in place of unplugged XDomain we
